---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import EntryList from '../components/EntryList.astro';
import { getArticles, getVideos } from '../lib/content';
import { getPosts } from '../lib/substack';
const favs = [
  ...(await getPosts()).slice(0, 3).map((p) => ({ title: p.title, href: `/articles/${p.slug}`, date: p.date, kind: 'Essay' })),
  ...(await getArticles()).filter((a) => a.data.featured).map((e) => ({ title: e.data.title, href: `/articles/${e.id}`, date: e.data.date, kind: 'Essay' })),
].sort((a, b) => b.date.valueOf() - a.date.valueOf());
---
<Base title="Start here" description="New here? The best places to begin.">
  <div class="page">
    <h1 class="title">Start here</h1>
    <p>Welcome. I’m KV, and this is my notebook: mental models, essays, books and projects, all following whatever I’m curious about. If you only read a few things, make it these.</p>
    <h2 class="sub-h">Favourites</h2>
    <EntryList rows={favs} />
    <h2 class="sub-h">Then</h2>
    <p class="measure">Browse the <a href="/models" class="u">models</a> I think with, follow a <a href="/series" class="u">series</a> from part one, see what I’m <a href="/projects" class="u">making</a>, or check what I’m doing <a href="/now" class="u">now</a>. The best way to keep up is the newsletter below.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
